 <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator-line c-mmp__indicator-line--buffered js-playback-buffered\" style=\"width:0%\"></span> <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator-line c-mmp__indicator-line--tracked js-playback-tracked\" style=\"width:0%\"></span> <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator-line c-mmp__indicator-line--played js-playback-played\" style=\"width:0%\"></span> <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator-line c-mmp__indicator-line--live js-playback-live\"><span class=\"strip\"></span></span> <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator-btn ta-c js-progressbar-btn\"> <button class=\"c-mmp__indicator-btn-pointer\" type=\"button\"></button> </span> <span class=\"c-mmp__badge c-mmp__badge--tracked-time c-mmp__badge--hidden js-progressbar-indicator-badge\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"left:0%\"> <span class=\"c-mmp__badge-text js-progressbar-indicator-badge-text\">0:00</span> </span> </span> </span> \n       </div> \n       <div class=\"c-mmp__cpanel-additional-controls\"> <span class=\"c-mmp__cpanel-additional-controls-volume js-volume-controls\"> <span class=\"c-mmp__cpanel-btn c-mmp__cpanel-btn--volume js-btn-volume\" title=\"volume\"> <span class=\"ico ico-volume-unmuted m-0\"></span> </span> <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator c-mmp__indicator--vertical js-volume-panel\" dir=\"ltr\"> <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator-lines js-volumebar\"> <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator-line c-mmp__indicator-line--range js-volume-range\" style=\"height:100%\"></span> <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator-line c-mmp__indicator-line--volume js-volume-level\" style=\"height:0%\"></span> <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator-slider\"> <span class=\"c-mmp__indicator-btn ta-c c-mmp__indicator-btn--hidden js-volumebar-btn\"> <button class=\"c-mmp__indicator-btn-pointer\" type=\"button\"></button> </span> </span> </span> </span> </span> \n        <div class=\"c-mmp__cpanel-additional-controls-settings js-settings-controls\"> <span class=\"c-mmp__cpanel-btn c-mmp__cpanel-btn--settings-overlay js-btn-settings-overlay\" title=\"source switch\"> <span class=\"ico ico-settings m-0\"></span> </span> <span class=\"c-mmp__cpanel-btn c-mmp__cpanel-btn--settings-expand js-btn-settings-expand\" title=\"source switch\"> <span class=\"ico ico-settings m-0\"></span> </span> \n         <div class=\"c-mmp__expander c-mmp__expander--sources js-c-mmp__expander--sources\"> \n          <div class=\"c-mmp__expander-content js-sources\"></div> \n         </div> \n        </div> \n       </div> \n      </div> \n     </div> \n    </div> \n   </div> \n  </div> \n  <div class=\"media-download\"> \n   <div class=\"simple-menu\"> <span class=\"handler\"> <span class=\"ico ico-download\"></span> <span class=\"label\">Faça o Download</span> <span class=\"ico ico-chevron-down\"></span> </span> \n    <div class=\"inner\"> \n     <ul class=\"subitems\"> \n      <li class=\"subitem\"> <a href=\"https://av.voanews.com/clips/VPO/2024/04/04/01000000-0a00-0242-61d3-08dc54d7147b_16k.mp3?download=1\" title=\"16 kbps | MP3\" class=\"handler\" onclick=\"FireAnalyticsTagEventOnDownload(this, \'audio\', 7557041, \'Candidatura presidencial aquece Comité Central da Frelimo que não tem o tema na agenda\', null, \'\', \'2024\', \'04\', \'04\')\"> 16 kbps | MP3 </a> </li> \n      <li class=\"subitem\"> <a href=\"https://av.voanews.com/clips/VPO/2024/04/04/01000000-0a00-0242-61d3-08dc54d7147b_32k.mp3?download=1\" title=\"32 kbps | MP3\" class=\"handler\" onclick=\"FireAnalyticsTagEventOnDownload(this, \'audio\', 7557041, \'Candidatura presidencial aquece Comité Central da Frelimo que não tem o tema na agenda\', null, \'\', \'2024\', \'04\', \'04\')\"> 32 kbps | MP3 </a> </li> \n      <li class=\"subitem\"> <a href=\"https://av.voanews.com/clips/VPO/2024/04/04/01000000-0a00-0242-61d3-08dc54d7147b_48k.mp3?download=1\" title=\"48 kbps | MP3\" class=\"handler\" onclick=\"FireAnalyticsTagEventOnDownload(this, \'audio\', 7557041, \'Candidatura presidencial aquece Comité Central da Frelimo que não tem o tema na agenda\', null, \'\', \'2024\', \'04\', \'04\')\"> 48 kbps | MP3 </a> </li> \n     </ul> \n    </div> \n   </div> \n  </div> <button class=\"btn btn--link btn-popout-player\" data-default-display=\"block\" data-popup-url=\"/pp/7557041/ppt0.html\" title=\"Janela de Pop-up\"> <span class=\"ico ico-arrow-top-right\"></span> <span class=\"text\">Janela de Pop-up</span> </button> \n </div> \n</div> \n<p><br> O braço feminino do partido no poder OMM deu na quara-feira, 3, o primeiro passo e traçou o perfil daquele que quer ver como o rosto dos camaradas para as próximas eleições presidenciais,.</p> \n<p>Isaura Nyusi, presidente da organização, deu o mote e numa mensagem para dentro do partido apontou o caminho e defendeu a necessidade de se conhecer o candidato de Frelimo.<br> <br> “É desejo de todo o cidadão moçambicano ter uma escolha genuína do candidato a Presidente da República, para nortear o destino deste belo Moçambique. É nossa responsabilidade conhecer melhor o histórico pessoal, profissional e Político do candidato, sua postura ética e a forma como ele se relaciona com a sociedade, como forma de assegurar a herança de uma boa governação e com é óbvio, desenvolvimento do país” disse a primeira-dama, apontando a seguir, o perfil que a OMM deseja.<br> <br> “O nosso candidato deve ter o perfil do povo para o povo, evitando o processo de mercantilismo e vaidade pessoal”, concluiu Isaura Nusi.<br> <br> Até há uma semana, a narrativa do partido era de que a escolha do candidato estava fora da agenda da terceira sessão do Comité Central, contudo, quando faltam dois dias para o arranque, a retórica mudou de tom.</p> \n<p>Admite-se que o assunto se tornou incontornável, mas, para já, oficialmente, ainda não há candidatos.<br> <br> “Ainda não há nenhum nome avançado, como temos estado a dizer”, disse Ludmila Magune, a porta-voz do partido, sinalizando a possibilidade da Comissão Política da Frelimo, tomar alguma decisão sobre o assunto.<br> <br> <strong>“Samito” adianta-se</strong><br> <br> Enquanto isso, Samora Machel Jr. quebrou os protocolos e anunciou a sua candidatura para as internas do partido.</p> \n<p>Através de um manifesto que tornou público através das redes sociais e da imprensa nacional, o primogénito de Samora Machel, primeiro Presidente de Moçambique, anunciou a sua pretensão de liderar o partido nas eleições de outubro, sendo o único que, até ao momento, se manifestou.<br> <br> “A minha candidatura é fundamentada nos princípios da busca pela paz, pelo respeito pela diversidade e pela diferença, promoção da inclusão e igualdade, dignidade humana e assegurar o crescimento económico de Moçambique para garantir um ambiente propício ao desenvolvimento económico e social, com especial atenção à criação de empregos para jovens e assistência aos mais necessitados. A minha candidatura é um misto de inquietações, mas também de esperança, visando dar respostas aos problemas e desejos dos moçambicanos”, indica o manifesto de Samora Machel Jr.<br> <br> Num debate promovido na quarta-feira, 3, pelo Centro de Integridade Pública, o politólogo José Jaime Macuane classificou a atitude de Samito, como é carinhosamente tratado Samora Machel Jr, de um passo estratégico.<br> <br> “Eu tenho a impressão de que, na correlação de forças, este passo é um passo estratégico de quem, eventualmente, sinta que, a não ser que seja ousado e dê este passo, estaria em desvantagem”, sustentou Macuane.<br> <br> Refira-se que ao nível da imprensa, há mais de cinco nomes de prováveis presidenciáveis que circulam, entre os quais, a antiga primeira-ministra, Luísa Diogo, os antigos ministros do Interior, José Pacheco e Basílio Monteiro, e o atual titular da paste da Agricultura e Desenvolvimento Rural, Celso Correia.</p>', 'Samora Machel Jr. anunciou a sua candidatura à liderança do partido e a Organização da Mulher Moçambicana já definiu o perfil do próximo líder', 38320, 0, '2024-04-04 14:47:15', '2024-04-04 15:01:17', 13);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (27585, 'L\'équipe kényanne réduite pour le marathon aux JO-2024', '<p>Par rapport aux 20 athlètes dont les noms avaient été initialement annoncés en décembre, seulement six de la dizaine de coureurs de fond hommes et femmes annoncés jeudi feront le déplacement à Paris.</p> \n<p>Kipchoge, 39 ans, fait partie de la liste tout comme le double vainqueur du marathon de Boston Benson Kipruto, Timothy Kiplagat et Vincent Kipkemboi Ngetich ainsi que Alexander Mutiso, deuxième du marathon de Berlin en 2023</p> \n<p>Kipchoge vise à obtenir une 3e médaille d\'or olympique après celles gagnées à Rio en 2016 et à Tokyo en 2021. Mais il a eu des difficultés à finir 10e au marathon de Tokyo le mois dernier, avec un temps de 2:06:50 loin du vainqueur, Kipruto, qui s\'est imposé en 2:02:16, et de son dauphin, Kiplagat, arrivé en 2:02:55.</p> \n<p>Le détenteur du record du monde Kelvin Kiptum, également Kenyan, est décédé dans un accident de voiture en février.</p> \n<p>Chez les femmes, Peres Jepchirchir, médaillée d\'or à Tokyo, et la médaillée d\'argent Brigid Kosgei feront partie de la délégation avec la gagnante des récents marathons de Boston et Chicago Helen Obiri. Rosemary Wanjiru, Sharon Lokedi et la championne du monde 2019 Ruth Chepngetich sont également présentes sur cette liste.</p> \n<p>\"<em>Le voyage commence alors que nous allons défendre notre couronne</em>\", a affirmé le comité olympique kényan sur X.</p> \n<p>Composition de la liste initiale pour la délégation du Kenya en athlétisme aux Jeux olympiques de Paris:</p> \n<p>Hommes: Eliud Kipchoge, Vincent Kipkemoi Ngetich, Timothy Kiplagat, Benson Kipruto, Alexander Mutiso.</p> \n<p>Femmes: Ruth Chepngetich, Brigid Kosgei, Helen Obiri, Rosemary Wanjiru, Sharon Lokedi, Peres Jepchirchir.</p>', 'Eliud Kipchoge, double médaillé d\'or olympique en titre en marathon, sera le fer de lance d\'une délégation du Kenya réduite dépêchée aux Jeux olympiques de Paris, avec la championne sortante Peres Jepchirchir, ont indiqué jeudi les responsables de l\'athlétisme kényans.', 36568, 0, '2024-04-04 14:53:23', '2024-04-04 16:00:30', 6);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (27586, 'Dividend Investors: Don\'t Be Too Quick To Buy Glacier Bancorp, Inc. (NYSE:GBCI) For Its Upcoming Dividend', '<p><strong>Glacier Bancorp, Inc.</strong> (<a href=\"https://au.finance.yahoo.com/quote/GBCI\" data-ylk=\"slk:NYSE:GBCI;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">NYSE:GBCI</a>) is about to trade ex-dividend in the next 3 days. The ex-dividend date is one business day before the record date, which is the cut-off date for shareholders to be present on the company\'s books to be eligible for a dividend payment. The ex-dividend date is of consequence because whenever a stock is bought or sold, the trade takes at least two business day to settle. Thus, you can purchase Glacier Bancorp\'s shares before the 8th of April in order to receive the dividend, which the company will pay on the 18th of April.</p>\n<p>The company\'s next dividend payment will be US$0.33 per share, on the back of last year when the company paid a total of US$1.32 to shareholders. Last year\'s total dividend payments show that Glacier Bancorp has a trailing yield of 3.5% on the current share price of US$37.81. If you buy this business for its dividend, you should have an idea of whether Glacier Bancorp\'s dividend is reliable and sustainable. So we need to check whether the dividend payments are covered, and if earnings are growing.</p>\n<p><span class=\"veryHighlightLink\"><a href=\"https://simplywall.st/company/id/BDDE420C-04F6-4EEB-AEFF-D5F602EE36E8?blueprint=2978175&amp;utm_medium=finance_user&amp;utm_campaign=cta&amp;utm_source=yahoo\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:See our latest analysis for Glacier Bancorp;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \"> See our latest analysis for Glacier Bancorp </a></span></p>\n<p>Dividends are usually paid out of company profits, so if a company pays out more than it earned then its dividend is usually at greater risk of being cut. Glacier Bancorp paid out more than half (66%) of its earnings last year, which is a regular payout ratio for most companies.</p>\n<div class=\"caas-da \">\n <div data-wf-benji-page-context=\"{&quot;pageUrl&quot;:&quot;https://sg.finance.yahoo.com/news/dividend-investors-dont-too-quick-191741378.html&quot;,&quot;spaceid&quot;:&quot;1187300073&quot;,&quot;site&quot;:&quot;finance&quot;,&quot;hashtag&quot;:&quot;earnings;investments;stocks;finance&quot;,&quot;lmsid&quot;:&quot;a0V0W00000HOZhrUAH&quot;,&quot;lpstaid&quot;:&quot;90b6255c-c925-380c-bfde-f89cf67d94c1&quot;,&quot;pct&quot;:&quot;story&quot;}\" data-wf-benji-wafer-config=\"{}\" data-wf-benji-config=\"{&quot;positions&quot;:{&quot;INARTICLE-90b6255c-c925-380c-bfde-f89cf67d94c11712260852664&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;INARTICLE-90b6255c-c925-380c-bfde-f89cf67d94c11712260852664&quot;,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;/22888152279/${REGION}/yfin/ros/dt/${REGION}_yfin_ros_dt_mid_center&quot;,&quot;region&quot;:&quot;index&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;fluid&quot;,&quot;kvs&quot;:{&quot;loc&quot;:&quot;mid_center&quot;},&quot;disableRefresh&quot;:true}}}\" id=\"sda-INARTICLE-90b6255c-c925-380c-bfde-f89cf67d94c11712260852664\" class=\"wafer-benji caas-sda-benji-ad\" data-wf-trigger=\"onLoad\" data-wf-margin=\"100 0\">\n  <div id=\"sdaAdvText-INARTICLE-90b6255c-c925-380c-bfde-f89cf67d94c11712260852664\" class=\"caas-sda-adv-text\">\n   ADVERTISEMENT\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"INARTICLE-90b6255c-c925-380c-bfde-f89cf67d94c11712260852664\"></div>\n </div>\n</div>\n<p>Companies that pay out less in dividends than they earn in profits generally have more sustainable dividends. The lower the payout ratio, the more wiggle room the business has before it could be forced to cut the dividend.</p>\n<p>Click <a href=\"https://simplywall.st/company/id/BDDE420C-04F6-4EEB-AEFF-D5F602EE36E8/dividend?blueprint=2978175&amp;utm_medium=finance_user&amp;utm_campaign=integrated-pitch&amp;utm_source=yahoo\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:here to see the company\'s payout ratio, plus analyst estimates of its future dividends.;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">here to see the company\'s payout ratio, plus analyst estimates of its future dividends.</a></p>\n<figure class=\"caas-figure\">\n <div class=\"caas-figure-with-pb\" style=\"max-height: 508px\">\n  <div>\n   <div class=\"caas-img-container caas-img-loader\" style=\"padding-bottom:62%\">\n    <a class=\"link\" href=\"https://simplywall.st/company/id/BDDE420C-04F6-4EEB-AEFF-D5F602EE36E8/dividend?blueprint=2978175&amp;utm_medium=finance_user&amp;utm_campaign=infographic&amp;utm_source=yahoo\" data-ylk><img class=\"caas-img caas-lazy\" alt=\"historic-dividend\" data-src=\"https://s.yimg.com/ny/api/res/1.2/cGiC1yCWvDSmNw04XSPVdA--/YXBwaWQ9aGlnaGxhbmRlcjt3PTk2MDtoPTU5NA--/https://media.zenfs.com/en/simply_wall_st__316/904dc63b9434592cf576f8e0284b351f\">\n     <noscript>\n      <img alt=\"historic-dividend\" src=\"https://s.yimg.com/ny/api/res/1.2/cGiC1yCWvDSmNw04XSPVdA--/YXBwaWQ9aGlnaGxhbmRlcjt3PTk2MDtoPTU5NA--/https://media.zenfs.com/en/simply_wall_st__316/904dc63b9434592cf576f8e0284b351f\" class=\"caas-img\">\n     </noscript></a>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </div>\n <div class=\"caption-wrapper caption-aligned-with-image\">\n  <figcaption class=\"caption-collapse\">\n   historic-dividend\n  </figcaption>\n </div>\n</figure>\n<h2>Have Earnings And Dividends Been Growing?</h2>\n<p>Businesses with shrinking earnings are tricky from a dividend perspective. Investors love dividends, so if earnings fall and the dividend is reduced, expect a stock to be sold off heavily at the same time. So we\'re not too excited that Glacier Bancorp\'s earnings are down 2.0% a year over the past five years.</p>\n<div class=\"caas-readmore caas-readmore-collapse\">\n <button class=\"link caas-button collapse-button\" data-ylk=\"elm:readmore;slk:Story continues\">Story continues</button>\n</div>\n<p>The main way most investors will assess a company\'s dividend prospects is by checking the historical rate of dividend growth. In the past 10 years, Glacier Bancorp has increased its dividend at approximately 8.2% a year on average. Growing the dividend payout ratio while earnings are declining can deliver nice returns for a while, but it\'s always worth checking for when the company can\'t increase the payout ratio any more - because then the music stops.</p>\n<h2>To Sum It Up</h2>\n<p>Should investors buy Glacier Bancorp for the upcoming dividend? Earnings per share have been declining and the company is paying out more than half its profits to shareholders; not an enticing combination. These characteristics don\'t generally lead to outstanding dividend performance, and investors may not be happy with the results of owning this stock for its dividend.</p>\n<p>Although, if you\'re still interested in Glacier Bancorp and want to know more, you\'ll find it very useful to know what risks this stock faces. Case in point: We\'ve spotted <a href=\"https://simplywall.st/company/id/BDDE420C-04F6-4EEB-AEFF-D5F602EE36E8?blueprint=2978175&amp;utm_medium=finance_user&amp;utm_campaign=conclusion&amp;utm_source=yahoo\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:2 warning signs for Glacier Bancorp;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \"><strong>2 warning signs for Glacier Bancorp</strong></a> you should be aware of.</p>\n<p>A common investing mistake is buying the first interesting stock you see. Here you can find <a href=\"https://simplywall.st/discover/investing-ideas/240709/top-dividend-stocks/global?blueprint=2978175&amp;utm_medium=finance_user&amp;utm_campaign=conclusion-grid&amp;utm_source=yahoo\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:a full list of high-yield dividend stocks.;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \"><strong>a full list of high-yield dividend stocks.</strong></a></p>\n<p><strong>Have feedback on this article? Concerned about the content?</strong> <a href=\"https://feedback.simplywall.st/article/Mjk3ODE3NTo1YjhjMGIxNWNhYTBjMzUy\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:Get in touch;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \"><strong>Get in touch</strong></a><strong> with us directly.</strong><i> Alternatively, email editorial-team (at) simplywallst.com.</i><br><br><i>This article by Simply Wall St is general in nature. <strong>We provide commentary based on historical data and analyst forecasts only using an unbiased methodology and our articles are not intended to be financial advice.</strong> It does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell any stock, and does not take account of your objectives, or your financial situation. We aim to bring you long-term focused analysis driven by fundamental data. Note that our analysis may not factor in the latest price-sensitive company announcements or qualitative material. Simply Wall St has no position in any stocks mentioned.</i></p>', NULL, 15033, 0, '2024-04-04 15:17:41', '2024-04-04 16:00:53', 10);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (27587, '3 Reasons Gold Prices Continue To Climb', '<p>Unless you’ve been living under a rock, it won’t have escaped your <a href=\"https://www.cityam.com/centamin-higher-gold-production-boosts-earnings-for-london-listed-miner/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:notice that gold is doing rather well.;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">notice that gold is doing rather well.</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.cityam.com/will-gold-continue-to-shine-in-2024/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:The safe haven asset has been stirred upwards as conflicts across the world have shown little to no sign of abating, and the four-year-long wait for interest rate cuts in the US and UK continues.;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">The safe haven asset has been stirred upwards as conflicts across the world have shown little to no sign of abating, and the four-year-long wait for interest rate cuts in the US and UK continues.</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.cityam.com/london-gold-price-benchmark-hits-record-high-as-investors-hunt-for-safe-haven/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:Yesterday, gold was trading near $2,250 (£1,788) per troy ounce and touching $2,288 (£1,818) today, another all-time record extending the record-setting days that have come in January, February and March this year.;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">Yesterday, gold was trading near $2,250 (£1,788) per troy ounce and touching $2,288 (£1,818) today, another all-time record extending the record-setting days that have come in January, February and March this year.</a></p>\n<p>But why is gold still rising?</p>\n<h2><strong>1.) Geopolitics drives investors to gold</strong></h2>\n<p>The wars in Ukraine and Gaza continue and the potential escalation to other countries keeps hanging over the markets like the sword of Damocles.</p>\n<div class=\"caas-da \">\n <div data-wf-benji-page-context=\"{&quot;pageUrl&quot;:&quot;https://sg.finance.yahoo.com/news/3-reasons-gold-prices-continue-190000467.html&quot;,&quot;spaceid&quot;:&quot;1187300073&quot;,&quot;site&quot;:&quot;finance&quot;,&quot;hashtag&quot;:&quot;marketsexchanges;commoditymarkets;investments;goldinvesting;finance;commoditymarkets&quot;,&quot;lmsid&quot;:&quot;a0Vd0000006tjbSEAQ&quot;,&quot;lpstaid&quot;:&quot;321e3df3-c14e-37b3-b04d-37efaf00c83e&quot;,&quot;pct&quot;:&quot;story&quot;}\" data-wf-benji-wafer-config=\"{}\" data-wf-benji-config=\"{&quot;positions&quot;:{&quot;INARTICLE-321e3df3-c14e-37b3-b04d-37efaf00c83e1712260853054&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;INARTICLE-321e3df3-c14e-37b3-b04d-37efaf00c83e1712260853054&quot;,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;/22888152279/${REGION}/yfin/ros/dt/${REGION}_yfin_ros_dt_mid_center&quot;,&quot;region&quot;:&quot;index&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;fluid&quot;,&quot;kvs&quot;:{&quot;loc&quot;:&quot;mid_center&quot;},&quot;disableRefresh&quot;:true}}}\" id=\"sda-INARTICLE-321e3df3-c14e-37b3-b04d-37efaf00c83e1712260853054\" class=\"wafer-benji caas-sda-benji-ad\" data-wf-trigger=\"onLoad\" data-wf-margin=\"100 0\">\n  <div id=\"sdaAdvText-INARTICLE-321e3df3-c14e-37b3-b04d-37efaf00c83e1712260853054\" class=\"caas-sda-adv-text\">\n   ADVERTISEMENT\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"INARTICLE-321e3df3-c14e-37b3-b04d-37efaf00c83e1712260853054\"></div>\n </div>\n</div>\n<p>Investors and governments are all too wary of another fallout akin to when Vladimir Putin first invaded Ukraine two years ago and gold is one of the most effective hedges against these concerns.</p>\n<p>Data from BullionVault, the world’s largest online precious metal marketplace, shows that Western investors banked record profits from selling gold in March, offloading almost twice the amount purchased.</p>\n<p>“Previous peaks in the number of people selling gold also came as bullion prices jumped, ” says BullionVault director of research Adrian Ash.</p>\n<p>“But they all coincided with moments of acute political or financial stress, spurring stronger investor demand.”</p>\n<p>Indeed sellers through the platform rose 95 per cent to beat the number recorded during the English riots and Euro debt crisis of 2011, March 2022 when Russia invaded Ukraine and the Brexit referendum shock in June 2016.</p>\n<p>In contrast, gold’s new all-time highs have grown exponentially as the general unease around global conflicts has continued.</p>\n<p>That, Ash says, “speaks to the underlying strength of this price uptrend”.</p>\n<h2><strong>2.) Central banks keep buying</strong></h2>\n<p>Strong physical demand from central banks and retail investors in Asia is also supporting the yellow metal. However, demand is expected to fall in the short term as investors baulk at higher prices.</p>\n<div class=\"caas-readmore caas-readmore-collapse\">\n <button class=\"link caas-button collapse-button\" data-ylk=\"elm:readmore;slk:Story continues\">Story continues</button>\n</div>\n<p>Ole Hansen, head of commodity strategy for Saxo, said that the prospect for lower funding costs may finally see demand for bullion-backed, exchange-traded funds (ETFs) from real money asset managers pick up for the first time since 2022.</p>\n<p>And though the buying rate is slowing, the world’s central banks are still stockpiling gold where they can.</p>\n<p>Figures from the World Gold Council show that reported global central bank gold reserves for February rose by 19 tonnes.</p>\n<p>Despite this being the ninth consecutive month of growth, the data show a slowdown, with buying for the month 58 per cent lower than January’s.</p>\n<p>On a year-to-date basis, central banks report the addition of 64 tonnes over January and February, 43 per cent lower than the same period in 2023 but a fourfold increase on 2022.</p>\n<h2><strong>3.) Gold as a hedge against inflation</strong></h2>\n<p>Gold rallies are frequently built around when inflation looks to be on an upward curve, depreciating the value of currency.</p>\n<p>An update on Federal Reserve Chairman Jerome Powell’s policy outlook, due this week, will be an important driver for stocks and commodities this week, however.</p>\n<p>The Fed is not cutting <a href=\"https://www.ft.com/content/088d3368-bb8b-4ff3-9df7-a7680d4d81b2\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:rates;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">rates</a> until June at the earliest and year-on-year inflation is sitting at 2.5 per cent on the back of a burgeoning economy.</p>\n<p>The resulting strength of the US dollar is complicating matters further for gold future-gazers.</p>\n<p>The currency has just tipped over a four month high, adding pressure to the gold market and muddying the landscape for those with bullion exposure.</p>\n<p>Kathleen Brooks, research director at XTB Trading, points out that gold might have reached its ceiling, short of a course-correction event such as further geopolitical escalation and could be due a correction.</p>\n<p>“Open interest on gold contracts appears to have peaked and the gold price is now 15 per cent above its 200-day simple moving average (SMA),” she said.</p>\n<p>“This suggests that it is at extreme levels and could be due a pullback.”</p>\n<p>By CityAM</p>\n<p><strong>More Top Reads From Oilprice.com:</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"caas-list caas-list-bullet\">\n <li><p><strong><a href=\"https://oilprice.com/Energy/Energy-General/Ex-BP-CEO-Browne-27-Trillion-Needed-to-Pivot-Climate-Crisis-into-Correction.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:Ex-BP CEO Browne: £2.7 Trillion Needed to Pivot Climate Crisis into Correction;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">Ex-BP CEO Browne: £2.7 Trillion Needed to Pivot Climate Crisis into Correction</a></strong></p></li>\n <li><p><strong><a href=\"https://oilprice.com/Geopolitics/International/Ukraine-Aid-Bill-Faces-High-Stakes-Showdown-in-Congress.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:Ukraine Aid Bill Faces High-Stakes Showdown in Congress;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">Ukraine Aid Bill Faces High-Stakes Showdown in Congress</a></strong></p></li>\n <li><p><strong><a href=\"https://oilprice.com/Energy/Natural-Gas/Uzbekistans-Natural-Gas-Crunch-Squeezes-State-Coffers.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:Uzbekistan\'s Natural Gas Crunch Squeezes State Coffers;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">Uzbekistan\'s Natural Gas Crunch Squeezes State Coffers</a></strong></p></li>\n</ul>\n<p><a href=\"https://oilprice.com/Metals/Gold/3-Reasons-Gold-Prices-Continue-To-Climb.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:Read this article on OilPrice.com;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">Read this article on OilPrice.com</a></p>', NULL, 54189, 0, '2024-04-04 15:00:00', '2024-04-04 16:00:53', 10);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (27588, '耶伦二度访华，向中国发出遏制产能过剩的强硬信息', '<p>美国财政部长珍妮特·耶伦（Janet Yellen）星期四（4月4日）抵达中国南方经济重镇广州，对中国进行她任内的第二次访问，旨在进一步稳定美中两大经济体之间的金融和经济关系，并带给中国一个强硬的信息：中国产能过剩，尤其在清洁能源产品上，而世界无法承受。<br> <br> 由于多年来的政府大规模补贴以及国内需求疲软，中国的电动车、电池、太阳能板、半导体和其他制造产品正在充斥全球市场。许多产品的全球价格暴跌，对其他国家的厂商造成巨大压力。<br> <br> 路透社报道说，一位美国财政部高级官员谈到中国在关键领域的产能过剩时说，“我们看到更多公司亏损的威胁，它们将不得不想方设法出售其产品。”<br> <br> 耶伦在从周五至下周一的与中国主要经济官员举行的一系列会谈中，将谋求传递她的观点，即产能过剩对中国是不健康的，引发美国、欧洲、日本、墨西哥和其他主要经济体不断增加的忧虑和抨击。<br> <br> 这位要求匿名的美国官员说，耶伦将向中国官员解释，“如果全球范围内出现贸易行动，这不是一个反华的事情，而是对他们政策的回应。”</p>\n<div data-owner-ct=\"Article\" data-inline=\"False\"> \n <div class=\"media-block also-read\"> <a class=\"img-wrap img-wrap--size-3 also-read__img\" href=\"/a/us-china-excess-capacity-ira-clean-energy-suniva-20240327/7546276.html\" title=\"耶伦：下次访华将把中国产能过剩列为关键讨论议题\"> <span class=\"thumb thumb16_9\"> \n    <noscript class=\"nojs-img\"> \n     <img src=\"https://gdb.voanews.com/00ee9ccc-8631-4cfd-bb5d-01ed49d7c6c2_w100_r1.jpg\" alt=\"2024年3月27日，美国财政部长耶伦在参观了位于佐治亚州诺克罗斯的太阳能电池制造商苏尼瓦后发表讲话。（法新社）\"> \n    </noscript> <img data-src=\"https://gdb.voanews.com/00ee9ccc-8631-4cfd-bb5d-01ed49d7c6c2_w100_r1.jpg\" alt=\"2024年3月27日，美国财政部长耶伦在参观了位于佐治亚州诺克罗斯的太阳能电池制造商苏尼瓦后发表讲话。（法新社）\"> </span> </a> \n  <div class=\"media-block__content also-read__body also-read__body--h\"> <a href=\"/a/us-china-excess-capacity-ira-clean-energy-suniva-20240327/7546276.html\" title=\"耶伦：下次访华将把中国产能过剩列为关键讨论议题\"> <span class=\"also-read__text--label\"> 请同时参阅： </span> <h4 class=\"media-block__title media-block__title--size-3 also-read__text p-0\"> 耶伦：下次访华将把中国产能过剩列为关键讨论议题 </h4> </a> \n  </div> \n </div> \n</div> \n<p>预计，耶伦将就清洁能源补贴和工业产能过剩问题向中国施压。耶伦最近强调，这些问题“损害了美国企业和工人，也损害了世界各地的企业和工人”。<br> <br> 不过，报道表示，北京看来仍在加倍努力在高科技领域投资加强制造能力，而这一做法越来越与其他国家产生冲突。<br> <br> 路透社援引一位美国前财政部及贸易代表办公室官员的分析说，问题的本质是其他国家是否想进口中国价格扭曲的产品，而与中国贸易重新紧张的局面已经形成。<br> <br> 在前往广州的途中，耶伦谢绝说明她是否会在与中国副总理何立峰等官员的会晤中提及征收新关税的威胁。不过，耶伦表示，拜登政府决意通过投资税收抵免发展美国在电动车、太阳能和其他清洁能源产品的供应链，而且她不愿排除采用其他方式保护这些产业。<br> <br> 美联社周四也报道说，美中存有一系列分歧，中国政府补贴电动车和太阳能板制造、贸易、社媒软件TikTok的归属、获取尖端芯片及国家安全等问题都对双方谨慎管控关系构成风险。<br> <br> 耶伦4月3日在前往中国途中在阿拉斯加州安克雷奇停留时对记者们说，“我们需要一个公平竞争的环境。我们对中国大规模投资一些产业造成产能过剩感到关切。”<br> <br> 耶伦没有排除在绿色能源领域采取进一步行动抗衡中国补贴的可能性。她补充说，“这不仅仅是美国，很多其他国家，包括墨西哥、欧洲、日本，都在感受到中国在这些产业的大规模投资的压力。”<br> <br> 耶伦最近曾指责中国让受到大量补贴的绿色能源产品在全球市场泛滥。她说，她希望向中国官员重申她的忧虑，即中国用廉价的太阳能板和电动车充斥全球市场，威胁了其他国家在这些领域发展的能力。<br> <br> 耶伦这次4月4日至9日的访问是对她去年7月访问北京的后续行动。那次访问达成双方启动两个经济工作小组以缓解紧张关系的成果。</p>\n<div data-owner-ct=\"Article\" data-inline=\"False\"> \n <div class=\"media-block also-read\"> <a class=\"img-wrap img-wrap--size-3 also-read__img\" href=\"/a/us-china-trade-expert-control-economy-20240116/7442702.html\" title=\"关于2024年美中经贸关系，你需要知道的几个关键问题\"> <span class=\"thumb thumb16_9\"> \n    <noscript class=\"nojs-img\"> \n     <img src=\"https://gdb.voanews.com/4e37b869-c16d-4895-adea-33388fcbabed_cx0_cy9_cw0_w100_r1.jpg\" alt=\"资料照：2023年11月15日，美国商务部长雷蒙多出席美国总统拜登与中国国家主席习近平在亚太经合组织领导人峰会间隙在加州费罗丽庄园举行的双边会晤。（路透社）\"> \n    </noscript> <img data-src=\"https://gdb.voanews.com/4e37b869-c16d-4895-adea-33388fcbabed_cx0_cy9_cw0_w100_r1.jpg\" alt=\"资料照：2023年11月15日，美国商务部长雷蒙多出席美国总统拜登与中国国家主席习近平在亚太经合组织领导人峰会间隙在加州费罗丽庄园举行的双边会晤。（路透社）\"> </span> </a> \n  <div class=\"media-block__content also-read__body also-read__body--h\"> <a href=\"/a/us-china-trade-expert-control-economy-20240116/7442702.html\" title=\"关于2024年美中经贸关系，你需要知道的几个关键问题\"> <span class=\"also-read__text--label\"> 请同时参阅： </span> <h4 class=\"media-block__title media-block__title--size-3 also-read__text p-0\"> 关于2024年美中经贸关系，你需要知道的几个关键问题 </h4> </a> \n  </div> \n </div> \n</div> \n<p>报道表示，耶伦此行正值美国大选年，民主党及共和党在中国问题上都变得更加强硬，集中批评中国对TikTok的所有权、新闻审查、人权记录、一系列针对美国的间谍活动，包括黑客攻击和使用高空间谍气球等等。<br> <br> 不过，就在4月2日，美国总统乔·拜登（Joe Biden）和中国领导人习近平进行了自去年11月会晤以来的首次电话。<br> <br> 耶伦4月3日对记者们说，她此行是在拜登与习近平2022年11月在印尼巴厘岛会晤之后，美中两国高层对话的继续。<br> <br> 她说：“我想大家都知道拜登总统昨天与习主席通了话，我此行会晤对方官员，应当被视为对话的继续，自从习主席和拜登总统在巴厘会晤后，我们一直在展开并且不断加深这一对话。拜登总统责成我争取稳定我们的经济关系，加深我们的沟通。过去一年、一年半来我们一直在这样做。这将是我第三次会晤我的对口官员何立峰副总理。”<br> <br> 一位在耶伦访问前向记者介绍情况的财政部高级官员表示，除了会晤中国经济大总管何立峰副总理和其他现任和前任中央政府官员外，耶伦还将与学生、教授和商界领袖见面。<br> <br> 她的访问首站是南方城市广州，并在那里停留两天。耶伦在广州将与经济专家举行圆桌会谈，讨论中国经济的挑战和机遇，她还将会晤美国商界领袖和广东省省长王伟中。<br> <br> “耶伦部长有兴趣倾听中国的各种声音，以更好地了解中国当前的动态，”这位美国财政部官员说。<br> <br> 在北京，耶伦将与北京大学的学生和教授以及一些中国的主要经济学家会面。她与中央政府官员的会晤将包括与中国央行行长和财政部长举行座谈。<br> <br> 耶伦还将在访问期间会见中国的二号官员、国务院总理李强。<br> <br> 美国财政部一位高级官员表示，此行的目的是加强耶伦已经为管理两国关系而进行的密集外交。自去年7月首次访华以来，耶伦和中国副总理何立峰已经成立了经济工作组和金融工作组。这些工作组讨论了两国面临的问题--例如中国的房地产危机或去年美国两家主要银行的倒闭--以及政策应对措施。<br> <br> 最近几周，美国和欧盟加大了对补贴以及中国商品产能过剩和廉价出口所造成的影响的关注。<br> <br> 耶伦在安克雷奇停留时还说：“我认为重要的是，在所有层级，对我而言，在副总理层级进行沟通，既讨论我们对两国关系的重视，也讨论我们的关切——并且同意我们需要有一个公平的竞争环境。”<br> <br> <br> <br> </p>', NULL, 93133, 0, '2024-04-04 09:51:52', '2024-04-04 17:00:00', 1);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (27589, 'Yellen enfrenta camino difícil ante el problema del exceso de capacidad de China', '<span class=\"dateline\">GUANGZHOU, CHINA —&nbsp;</span> \n<p>La secretaria del Tesoro de Estados Unidos, Janet Yellen, viajaba este jueves a Guangzhou, el centro fabril del sur de China, con un duro mensaje para los funcionarios chinos: están produciendo demasiado de todo, especialmente bienes de energía limpia, y el mundo no puede absorberlo.</p> \n<p>China está desatando una avalancha de vehículos eléctricos, baterías, paneles solares, semiconductores y otros productos manufacturados en los mercados globales, resultado de años de enormes subsidios gubernamentales y una débil demanda interna.</p> \n<p>Los precios globales de muchos bienes se están hundiendo, presionando a los productores de otros países.</p> \n<p>\"Vemos una creciente amenaza de que las empresas pierdan dinero y tengan que vender su producción en alguna parte\", dijo un alto funcionario del Tesoro de Estados Unidos sobre la sobreproducción en sectores chinos clave.</p> \n<p>En una serie de reuniones con altos funcionarios económicos chinos del viernes al lunes, Yellen intentará transmitir su opinión de que el exceso de producción no es saludable para China y que hay una creciente preocupación al respecto en Estados Unidos, Europa, Japón y México, y otras economías importantes.</p> \n<p>El funcionario, que habló bajo condición de anonimato, añadió que Yellen explicaría: \"Si hay acciones comerciales en todo el mundo, no es algo anti-China, es una respuesta a sus políticas\".</p>\n<div data-owner-ct=\"Article\" data-inline=\"False\"> \n <div class=\"media-block also-read\"> <a class=\"img-wrap img-wrap--size-3 also-read__img\" href=\"/a/yellen-advierte-que-confrontara-a-china-por-sus-subsidios-energeticos/7547051.html\" title=\"Yellen advierte que confrontará a China por sus subsidios energéticos\"> <span class=\"thumb thumb16_9\"> \n    <noscript class=\"nojs-img\"> \n     <img src=\"https://gdb.voanews.com/6f1ded26-67af-4341-8f57-57cb7e700445_cx0_cy7_cw0_w100_r1.jpg\" alt=\"ARCHIVO - La secretaria del Tesoro de Estados Unidos, Janet Yellen, se dirige al Club Económico de Chicago en Chicago, Illinois, el 25 de enero de 2024. (Foto de KAMIL KRZACZYNSKI / AFP)\"> \n    </noscript> <img data-src=\"https://gdb.voanews.com/6f1ded26-67af-4341-8f57-57cb7e700445_cx0_cy7_cw0_w100_r1.jpg\" alt=\"ARCHIVO - La secretaria del Tesoro de Estados Unidos, Janet Yellen, se dirige al Club Económico de Chicago en Chicago, Illinois, el 25 de enero de 2024. (Foto de KAMIL KRZACZYNSKI / AFP)\"> </span> </a> \n  <div class=\"media-block__content also-read__body also-read__body--h\"> <a href=\"/a/yellen-advierte-que-confrontara-a-china-por-sus-subsidios-energeticos/7547051.html\" title=\"Yellen advierte que confrontará a China por sus subsidios energéticos\"> <span class=\"also-read__text--label\"> También lea </span> <h4 class=\"media-block__title media-block__title--size-3 also-read__text p-0\"> Yellen advierte que confrontará a China por sus subsidios energéticos </h4> </a> \n  </div> \n </div> \n</div> \n<p>Pero Beijing parece estar redoblando su apuesta por invertir en más capacidad manufacturera en sus sectores favorecidos de alta tecnología, una postura que también está cada vez más en desacuerdo con la Unión Europea, Japón, México y otras economías importantes.</p> \n<p>\"Creo que el escenario está preparado para renovadas tensiones con China\", dijo Brad Setser, ex funcionario comercial tanto del Tesoro de Estados Unidos como de la oficina del Representante Comercial de Estados Unidos. \"Es una cuestión intrínseca si otros países quieren importar las distorsiones de China\".</p> \n<p>Setser añadió que las advertencias de Yellen sobre la sobreproducción china pueden ser un paso inicial de la administración Biden hacia nuevos aranceles u otras barreras comerciales sobre los vehículos eléctricos, las baterías y otros productos chinos.</p> \n<p>De camino a Guangzhou, Yellen se negó a decir si plantearía la amenaza de nuevos aranceles en sus reuniones en Guangzhou y Beijing con el viceprimer ministro chino He Lifeng y el gobernador de la provincia de Guangdong, Wang Weizhong, quien también ha presidido sobre cientos de miles de millones de dólares en nuevos proyectos recientes.</p> \n<p>Pero dijo que la administración <em><strong><a class=\"wsw__a\" href=\"https://www.vozdeamerica.com/a/6856038.html\" target=\"_blank\">Biden estaba decidida a desarrollar cadenas de suministro estadounidenses</a></strong></em> en vehículos eléctricos, energía solar y otros bienes de energía limpia con créditos fiscales a la inversión y no \"descartaría otras formas posibles en las que los protegeríamos\".</p> \n<p>En marzo, los dirigentes de China se comprometieron a seguir adelante con el nuevo mantra del presidente Xi Jinping de desencadenar \"nuevas fuerzas productivas\" en China invirtiendo en el desarrollo de industrias tecnológicas, incluidos vehículos eléctricos, nuevos materiales, vuelos espaciales comerciales y ciencias de la vida, áreas en las que muchas empresas estadounidenses tienen ventajas.</p> \n<p><em><strong>¡Conéctate con la Voz de América! Suscríbete a nuestros canales de <a class=\"wsw__a\" href=\"https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fredirect%3Fevent%3Dvideo_description%26redir_token%3DQUFFLUhqa0NnRmlwS0luajhoQjlQT05lLXNVWXdadTNCUXxBQ3Jtc0ttLW1XeUJ2X3dMc0dPQTFWdWtoNkFjNFdwd2tzQUJTY2FpcW9NMEtCUnZVSHpJVGM0UUxMZzJrY1YyclNBM1pqTEhDM0tfdFE0SVExZkxVUnhUZ2ExZFFYTHphdzJIb1ZsbXJ0N0UwTWhLQ0YyaENSQQ%26q%3Dhttp%253A%252F%252Fbit.ly%252F2XpJNZj&amp;data=05%7C01%7Cgocando%40associates.voanews.com%7C85e4290da0bc44559b1208db9a78d6f3%7Cba99e87c673541c2b1c1354eee3a8659%7C0%7C0%7C638273616021819023%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=kRr%2FwDwZSW6a2HxHlKx5fTtATO%2FHLLvji8ystpk3eL4%3D&amp;reserved=0\">YouTube</a>, <a class=\"wsw__a\" href=\"https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fchat.whatsapp.com%2FDXySZH8uwGCECxTdlELdDI&amp;data=05%7C01%7Cgocando%40associates.voanews.com%7C85e4290da0bc44559b1208db9a78d6f3%7Cba99e87c673541c2b1c1354eee3a8659%7C0%7C0%7C638273616021819023%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=0MBdqzsmJDCVgwQncezbUiCRCNCmmG51tGMAXbi%2BjOA%3D&amp;reserved=0\">WhatsApp</a> y al <a class=\"wsw__a\" href=\"https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.vozdeamerica.com%2FSubscribe.html&amp;data=05%7C01%7Cgocando%40associates.voanews.com%7C85e4290da0bc44559b1208db9a78d6f3%7Cba99e87c673541c2b1c1354eee3a8659%7C0%7C0%7C638273616021819023%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=Q9jqLLDg50OBNGlZK6ape%2BdbsolE4ufhSGg5osg3E90%3D&amp;reserved=0\">newsletter</a>. Activa las notificaciones y síguenos en <a class=\"wsw__a\" href=\"https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2FVozdeAmerica%2F&amp;data=05%7C01%7Cgocando%40associates.voanews.com%7C85e4290da0bc44559b1208db9a78d6f3%7Cba99e87c673541c2b1c1354eee3a8659%7C0%7C0%7C638273616021819023%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=vkGAj%2BhlF7OakeTgL2O6e%2B7hDX%2BXx8%2FlWr1%2BVOyw7oI%3D&amp;reserved=0\">Facebook</a>, <a class=\"wsw__a\" href=\"https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Ftwitter.com%2FVozdeAmerica&amp;data=05%7C01%7Cgocando%40associates.voanews.com%7C85e4290da0bc44559b1208db9a78d6f3%7Cba99e87c673541c2b1c1354eee3a8659%7C0%7C0%7C638273616021819023%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=04xnVnq2F8KoAHEU5uUVoa6D0cygxmA%2FUeuEtKVON8U%3D&amp;reserved=0\">X</a> e <a class=\"wsw__a\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/vozdeamerica/\">Instagram</a>.</strong></em></p> \n<ul> \n</ul>', 'La secretaria del Tesoro de Estados Unidos viaja al centro fabril del sur de China, en medio de avalancha de producción de productos manufacturados en los mercados globales.', 33166, 0, '2024-04-04 15:52:10', '2024-04-04 17:00:23', 5);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (27590, 'NY株続落、530ドル安＝中東緊張やFRB高官発言で', '<p>　【ニューヨーク時事】4日のニューヨーク株式相場は4日続落した。中東の地政学的緊張の高まりに加え、米連邦準備制度理事会（FRB）高官から早期の利下げ開始に懐疑的な発言が相次いだことが嫌気された。優良株で構成するダウ工業株30種平均は前日終値比530．16ドル安の3万8596．98ドルで終了。ハイテク株中心のナスダック総合指数は228．38ポイント安の1万6049．08で引けた。　</p>', NULL, 57462, 0, '2024-04-04 17:00:46', '2024-04-04 17:00:46', 8);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (27591, 'ADENTRA\'s (TSE:ADEN) Dividend Will Be $0.14', '<p><strong>ADENTRA Inc.</strong> (<a href=\"https://au.finance.yahoo.com/quote/ADEN.TO\" data-ylk=\"slk:TSE:ADEN;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \">TSE:ADEN</a>) will pay a dividend of $0.14 on the 26th of April. Despite this raise, the dividend yield of 1.4% is only a modest boost to shareholder returns.</p>\n<p>While the dividend yield is important for income investors, it is also important to consider any large share price moves, as this will generally outweigh any gains from distributions. Investors will be pleased to see that ADENTRA\'s stock price has increased by 33% in the last 3 months, which is good for shareholders and can also explain a decrease in the dividend yield.</p>\n<p><span class=\"veryHighlightLink\"><a href=\"https://simplywall.st/company/id/8E6C1467-A4A1-4EAE-9095-902436800A41?blueprint=2978205&amp;utm_medium=finance_user&amp;utm_campaign=cta&amp;utm_source=yahoo\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:Check out our latest analysis for ADENTRA;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \"> Check out our latest analysis for ADENTRA </a></span></p>\n<h2>ADENTRA\'s Earnings Easily Cover The Distributions</h2>\n<p>While yield is important, another factor to consider about a company\'s dividend is whether the current payout levels are feasible. Before making this announcement, ADENTRA was easily earning enough to cover the dividend. As a result, a large proportion of what it earned was being reinvested back into the business.</p>\n<div class=\"caas-da \">\n <div data-wf-benji-page-context=\"{&quot;pageUrl&quot;:&quot;https://sg.finance.yahoo.com/news/adentras-tse-aden-dividend-0-195428746.html&quot;,&quot;spaceid&quot;:&quot;1187300073&quot;,&quot;site&quot;:&quot;finance&quot;,&quot;hashtag&quot;:&quot;investments;stocks;finance&quot;,&quot;lmsid&quot;:&quot;a0V0W00000HOZhrUAH&quot;,&quot;lpstaid&quot;:&quot;96aeaa64-e588-355e-bafb-886507fe0d80&quot;,&quot;pct&quot;:&quot;story&quot;}\" data-wf-benji-wafer-config=\"{}\" data-wf-benji-config=\"{&quot;positions&quot;:{&quot;INARTICLE-96aeaa64-e588-355e-bafb-886507fe0d801712264456863&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;INARTICLE-96aeaa64-e588-355e-bafb-886507fe0d801712264456863&quot;,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;/22888152279/${REGION}/yfin/ros/dt/${REGION}_yfin_ros_dt_mid_center&quot;,&quot;region&quot;:&quot;index&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;fluid&quot;,&quot;kvs&quot;:{&quot;loc&quot;:&quot;mid_center&quot;},&quot;disableRefresh&quot;:true}}}\" id=\"sda-INARTICLE-96aeaa64-e588-355e-bafb-886507fe0d801712264456863\" class=\"wafer-benji caas-sda-benji-ad\" data-wf-trigger=\"onLoad\" data-wf-margin=\"100 0\">\n  <div id=\"sdaAdvText-INARTICLE-96aeaa64-e588-355e-bafb-886507fe0d801712264456863\" class=\"caas-sda-adv-text\">\n   ADVERTISEMENT\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"INARTICLE-96aeaa64-e588-355e-bafb-886507fe0d801712264456863\"></div>\n </div>\n</div>\n<p>The next year is set to see EPS grow by 119.4%. If the dividend continues along recent trends, we estimate the payout ratio will be 17%, which is in the range that makes us comfortable with the sustainability of the dividend.</p>\n<figure class=\"caas-figure\">\n <div class=\"caas-figure-with-pb\" style=\"max-height: 508px\">\n  <div>\n   <div class=\"caas-img-container caas-img-loader\" style=\"padding-bottom:62%\">\n    <a class=\"link\" href=\"https://simplywall.st/company/id/8E6C1467-A4A1-4EAE-9095-902436800A41/dividend?blueprint=2978205&amp;utm_medium=finance_user&amp;utm_campaign=infographic&amp;utm_source=yahoo\" data-ylk><img class=\"caas-img caas-lazy\" alt=\"historic-dividend\" data-src=\"https://s.yimg.com/ny/api/res/1.2/mg4RyxCygBBRvUcDMH2v7A--/YXBwaWQ9aGlnaGxhbmRlcjt3PTk2MDtoPTU5NA--/https://media.zenfs.com/en/simply_wall_st__316/c161078b727ec46d3e1c5bd369b41bc9\">\n     <noscript>\n      <img alt=\"historic-dividend\" src=\"https://s.yimg.com/ny/api/res/1.2/mg4RyxCygBBRvUcDMH2v7A--/YXBwaWQ9aGlnaGxhbmRlcjt3PTk2MDtoPTU5NA--/https://media.zenfs.com/en/simply_wall_st__316/c161078b727ec46d3e1c5bd369b41bc9\" class=\"caas-img\">\n     </noscript></a>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </div>\n <div class=\"caption-wrapper caption-aligned-with-image\">\n  <figcaption class=\"caption-collapse\">\n   historic-dividend\n  </figcaption>\n </div>\n</figure>\n<h2>ADENTRA Has A Solid Track Record</h2>\n<p>The company has been paying a dividend for a long time, and it has been quite stable which gives us confidence in the future dividend potential. The dividend has gone from an annual total of $0.132 in 2014 to the most recent total annual payment of $0.411. This implies that the company grew its distributions at a yearly rate of about 12% over that duration. So, dividends have been growing pretty quickly, and even more impressively, they haven\'t experienced any notable falls during this period.</p>\n<h2>ADENTRA Could Grow Its Dividend</h2>\n<p>Some investors will be chomping at the bit to buy some of the company\'s stock based on its dividend history. We are encouraged to see that ADENTRA has grown earnings per share at 8.2% per year over the past five years. A low payout ratio and decent growth suggests that the company is reinvesting well, and it also has plenty of room to increase the dividend over time.</p>\n<div class=\"caas-readmore caas-readmore-collapse\">\n <button class=\"link caas-button collapse-button\" data-ylk=\"elm:readmore;slk:Story continues\">Story continues</button>\n</div>\n<h2>We Really Like ADENTRA\'s Dividend</h2>\n<p>In summary, it is always positive to see the dividend being increased, and we are particularly pleased with its overall sustainability. Distributions are quite easily covered by earnings, which are also being converted to cash flows. Taking this all into consideration, this looks like it could be a good dividend opportunity.</p>\n<p>Investors generally tend to favour companies with a consistent, stable dividend policy as opposed to those operating an irregular one. However, there are other things to consider for investors when analysing stock performance. For example, we\'ve identified <a href=\"https://simplywall.st/company/id/8E6C1467-A4A1-4EAE-9095-902436800A41?blueprint=2978205&amp;utm_medium=finance_user&amp;utm_campaign=conclusion&amp;utm_source=yahoo\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:2 warning signs for ADENTRA;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \"><strong>2 warning signs for ADENTRA</strong></a> (1 doesn\'t sit too well with us!) that you should be aware of before investing. Is ADENTRA not quite the opportunity you were looking for? Why not check out our <a href=\"https://simplywall.st/discover/investing-ideas/240709/top-dividend-stocks/global?blueprint=2978205&amp;utm_medium=finance_user&amp;utm_campaign=conclusion-grid&amp;utm_source=yahoo\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:selection of top dividend stocks.;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \"><strong>selection of top dividend stocks. </strong></a></p>\n<p><strong>Have feedback on this article? Concerned about the content?</strong> <a href=\"https://feedback.simplywall.st/article/Mjk3ODIwNTpjNWRmODFjY2RmODZiZWIz\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\" data-ylk=\"slk:Get in touch;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas\" class=\"link \"><strong>Get in touch</strong></a><strong> with us directly.</strong><i> Alternatively, email editorial-team (at) simplywallst.com.</i><br><br><i>This article by Simply Wall St is general in nature. <strong>We provide commentary based on historical data and analyst forecasts only using an unbiased methodology and our articles are not intended to be financial advice.</strong> It does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell any stock, and does not take account of your objectives, or your financial situation. We aim to bring you long-term focused analysis driven by fundamental data. Note that our analysis may not factor in the latest price-sensitive company announcements or qualitative material. Simply Wall St has no position in any stocks mentioned.</i></p>', NULL, 48244, 0, '2024-04-04 15:54:28', '2024-04-04 17:00:57', 10);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (27592, '【美股盤後】收黑', '<p>（中央社台北2024年4月5日電）在市場憂心中東局勢促使國際油價上漲的情況下，華爾街股市主要指數今天由紅翻黑，收盤前重挫。</p>\n<p>道瓊工業指數挫跌530.16點或1.36%，以38596.98點作收。</p>\n<p>標準普爾500指數下挫64.28點或1.23%，收5147.21點。</p>\n<p>科技股那斯達克指數下跌228.38點或1.40%，收16049.08點。</p>\n<p>費城半導體指數重挫147.43點或3.01%，收4756.07點。</p>', NULL, 71410, 0, '2024-04-04 16:51:48', '2024-04-04 18:00:14', 3);
